  "result": "Fixed in `src/click/types.py`: `IntRange._clamp` moved in the wrong direction for open bounds.\n\n`dir` is the direction to move back into the range (1 for a lower bound, -1 for an upper bound), but the code did `bound - dir`. With `min_open=True`, a value at or below the minimum clamped to `min - 1`, still out of range. With `max_open=True`, it clamped to `max + 1`. It now returns `bound + dir`, so open bounds clamp to `min + 1` / `max - 1`. Closed bounds were unaffected.\n\nI haven't run the test suite.",
